    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d817">

                <pb facs="0677" n="561" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg561"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12479.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chilean Chargé d’Affaires
                        to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 560.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chilean Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 10, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I hereby perform the pleasant duty of
                    transcribing to your excellency the telegram which I received from the Minister
                    of Foreigi Affairs of Chile, dated to-day, as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>His Excellency the President of the Republic instructs me to ask you
                            kindly to express to His Excellency President Wilson the profound
                            satisfaction with which the Government and people of Chile received,
                            through Minister Fletcher the cordial message<anchor n="51"
                                xml:id="d817-f1"/> which His Excellency the President of the United
                            States saw fit to send them, in which he expresses the gratitude of the
                            American Government and people for the friendly offices offered by my
                            Government in connection with the Argentine and Brazilian Governments on
                            the occasion of the controversy which arose between the United States
                            and the Government of Genera Huerta in Mexico, while referring to the
                            favorable judgment elicited by the action of our representative at the
                            Niagara Falls conferences.</p>
                        <p>You will likewise express to His Excellency Mr. Wilson the keen pleasure
                            with which the Government and people of Chile received the news of the
                            successful settlement of the differences which gave rise to the
                            mediation intended to obviate the painful consequences of an armed
                            conflict, and you will add that the cordial friendship which binds our
                            two countries together has been substantially strengthened by this new
                            bond of confraternity created by the act of mediation.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Enrique Villegas</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi>.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I beg of your excellency to kindly bring the contents of the foregoing telegram
                    to the knowledge of His Excellency President Wilson.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Antonio B. Agacio</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
